                    <!-- Authentication Guide -->
                    <h3>Authentication Guide</h3>
                    <p>To access protected endpoints, you must include your Access Token in the HTTP
                        <code>Authorization</code>
                        header of your requests.
                    </p>

                    <div class="well">
                        <p>Header Format:</p>
                        <p><code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN&gt;</code></p>
                    </div>

                    <p>Obtaining a Token Programmatically:</p>
                    <p>If you need to retrieve a token programmatically (e.g., from a script or server), you can use the
                        authentication endpoint:</p>
                    <pre style="background-color: #272822; color: #f8f8f2; padding: 15px; border-radius: 5px;">curl -X POST "{{baseUrl}}auth/login" \
     -H "Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded" \
     -d "username=YOUR_EMAIL" \
     -d 'password=YOUR_PASSWORD'</pre>

                    <p><strong>Example 1 (API Discovery):</strong></p>
                    <p class="small text-muted">Retrieve the list of all available data groups and domains.</p>
                    <pre style="background-color: #272822; color: #f8f8f2; padding: 15px; border-radius: 5px;">curl -X GET "{{baseUrl}}en/groupsanddomains" \
     -H "Authorization: Bearer &lt;YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN&gt;"</pre>

                    <p><strong>Example 2 (Data Retrieval):</strong></p>
                    <p class="small text-muted">Retrieve wheat production (element: 2510, item: 15) for Italy (area:106)
                        in 2022 from the Crops and Livestock Products domain (QCL).</p>
                    <pre id="curl-example"
                        style="background-color: #272822; color: #f8f8f2; padding: 15px; border-radius: 5px;">curl -X GET "{{baseUrl}}en/data/QCL?area=106&item=15&element=2510&year=2022" \
     -H "Authorization: Bearer &lt;YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN&gt;"</pre>

